---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "No Closing Cost Refinance (What it really means)";
const description =
  "Understand how no-closing-cost refinance offers work and how to compare them. Educational use only.";

const lastUpdated = "2026-01-31";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/refinance-no-closing-costs-myth" robots="noindex, follow" lastUpdated={lastUpdated}>
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">No closing cost</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>No closing cost refinance: what it really means</h1>
    <p>
      "No closing cost" usually means the lender is charging a higher rate or rolling costs into the loan. This guide helps you
      compare a no-closing-cost offer to a standard offer on the same time horizon.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/guides/refinance-break-even">Refinance break-even</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/refinance-closing-costs">Rolling costs into the loan</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/refinance">Refinance topic hub</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common structures</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Higher rate with lender credits that cover costs.</li>
      <li>Costs rolled into the new loan balance.</li>
      <li>Partial credits that reduce, but do not eliminate, cash-to-close.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">How to compare offers</h2>
    <ol class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Get the full fee list for each offer.</li>
      <li>Compare payments and total interest over your time horizon.</li>
      <li>Check whether the higher rate costs more than the upfront fees.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Inputs to request</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Rate with and without lender credits.</li>
      <li>Itemized closing costs and prepaid items.</li>
      <li>Cash-to-close estimate for each scenario.</li>
      <li>Expected time you will keep the new loan.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Decision checklist</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Compare total cost over your time horizon.</li>
      <li>Check whether the higher rate costs more than fees.</li>
      <li>Separate prepaid items from lender fees.</li>
      <li>Re-run if the rate or credits change.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Assuming no costs means no tradeoff.</li>
      <li>Not comparing to a standard offer with the same term.</li>
      <li>Ignoring that a higher rate increases interest every month.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Cash-to-close breakdown</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Separate lender fees from prepaid taxes and insurance.</li>
      <li>Confirm if credits can cover only lender fees or also prepaids.</li>
      <li>Track the net loan amount after credits and roll-ins.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Can no-closing-cost be the best option?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Yes, especially if you plan to move or refinance again before break-even.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Is a lender credit the same as free?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      No. Credits are often tied to a higher rate. Compare total cost across your horizon.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/apr-calculator">APR calculator</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/refinance-closing-costs">Refinance closing costs</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/discount-points-vs-lender-credits">Discount points vs lender credits</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/refinance-checklist">Refinance checklist</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/guides/refinance-break-even">Break-even guide</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/refinance">Refinance topic hub</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/refinance-checklist">Refinance checklist</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-01-31</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>



